  "frozenScientificReasoning": "## HB97 — HOLD on whole-inventory count/granularity plausibility\n\nThe frozen extraction contains exactly **97 records in 20 passages**; this is a verified file count. It is not a defensible count of 97 distinct, faithfully transcribed official competencies. I do not supply a replacement numerical count or a repaired extraction in this review.\n\nHB-C01 — source identity/granularity. Many remaining rows and passages are editorial summaries labelled `granularity: officialCompetencyBullet`, with rawSourceText simply repeating the authored summary. Different legitimate aggregation levels could produce different counts, but calling a summary an official bullet requires traceable original fragments and a stated aggregation policy. The actual full PDF also contains the S1–S17, E1–E12, K1–K13, B1–B14 standards, shared process/digital duties and content-table process duties; the current thematic inventory cannot be declared whole solely because its record count seems plausible.\n\nHB-C02 — invented/changed subject duty. Row index 39, ID ending `kinetik-045-9b33e04d`, assigns an LK official bullet about Arrhenius and autocatalysis. Actual page 24 instead explicitly gives LK reaction order from concentration-time data and SN1/SN2 mechanisms. Neither Arrhenius nor autocatalysis appears in the complete official PDF text. These may be teachable extensions but are not that official bullet. Their positive D/P quality would not repair the source claim.\n\nHB-C03 — incorrect GK/LK scope. Index 58 `energetik-064-ba40144b` labels entropy/Gibbs qualitative use GK_LK; index 59 `energetik-065-6a7ea7e8` does likewise for endergonic/exergonic processes and adds coupling. On actual page 30 the entropy, Gibbs and exergonic/endergonic terminology and competencies are in **LK**. Index 62 `elektrochemie-068-37c5d9b7` labels quantitative Faraday use GK_LK, whereas actual page 31 explicitly places Faraday calculations in **LK**. These are current source-fidelity defects regardless of a broader SkillPilot target.\n\nHB-C04 — optional context promoted to mandatory depth. Index 73 `kunststoffe-079-7418c562` labels silicone/conductive-polymer comparison an LK official bullet. Actual page 34 lists silicones in the thin-framed optional Vertiefungen, while the thick-framed LK content concerns radical-polymerization/esterification mechanisms and nanotechnology's property effects. Conductive plastics are not found in the complete official PDF text. This source record cannot make the optional silicone context a universal official LK duty.\n\nHB-C05 — duplicate/unequal allocation. Index 44 `kohlenhydrate-050-f975913c` now combines actual page-27 explanation of electrophoretic/TLC separation and determination/interpretation of Rf; index 50 `aminosaeuren-proteine-056-9091e6b6` again contains the same explanation bullet. Retaining an old ID may be technically appropriate, but the pair is overlapping allocation with different aggregation sizes, not two distinct independent obligations. The count must disclose this rather than use 97 as a count of unique official bullets. Neither a D keep nor correcting the Rf operator resolves whole-inventory granularity.\n\nHB-C06 — whole theme/selection context. Page 37 makes themes 1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 3.1, 3.2, 3.3 and 4.1 compulsory in all courses; theme 4.3 is additionally compulsory in LK. Of themes 2.1, 2.2, 2.3 and 4.2, one is required in GK and two in LK, with examination focus rules. On pages 15/21 thick frames distinguish binding competencies/terms/processes from thin optional contexts and experiments. Current broader inclusion of authored content in SkillPilot is allowed, but does not change these official choices or prove that a learner selected a theme. Rows 77/78 treating an invented LK-only advanced dye grouping or industrial-history assessment as literal page-35 bullets further illustrate the unresolved source/target distinction; page 35 has no separate LK content block.\n\nThe two positive exact page-36 source-row decisions above remain independently useful. They do not cure these other HB rows or justify whole-HB source acceptance. Required next work is a source-author reconstruction of original fragments, operators, LK/common status, theme choice, optional contexts, aggregation and overlap with a fresh independent review of the resulting exact inventory. This reviewer makes no author/source edits and grants no global/source/gate approval.\n",
